# A missing hashed asset must return a real 404, never the SPA shell.
# The bare catch-all below answered every stale-asset request with index.html
# (status 200, Content-Type: text/html) — for a module script that is the
# "Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the server responded with a
# MIME type of text/html" failure. A deploy swaps the whole hashed-asset set,
# so any tab holding the previous shell trips this the moment it asks for a
# hash the new deployment no longer contains. Static assets always win over
# redirect rules; only genuinely missing /assets/* paths reach the 404 rule.
/assets/* /404.html 404

/*  /index.html  200